<h1>Hardware Settings - Localiser (Metris MCA Advanced Settings)</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>When Metris MCA localiser is connected to the PC, click the Advanced Settings button and the following dialog will appear:</p>
<p><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/MCA_advanced_settings.gif" width="303px" height="224px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head" style="background-color:Transparent;">COM Port</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">Choose the COM port where the MetrisMCA arm is connected.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head" style="background-color:Transparent;">Button assignment section:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle" style="background-color:Transparent;">Blue to B, Red to A / Blue to A, Red to B</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">Mapping of Metris MCA blue and red buttons to KUBE software control A and B buttons (used respectively for Capture and FInish when taking data). The red and gray buttons of the handgrip provide the same functionality as the red and blue arm buttons respectively.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle" style="background-color:Transparent;">Axis end stop notification</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">Check the Enable box to switch ON the sound notification in case the arm reaches its end stop position while capturing data.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Probe_settings"></a>Probe settings</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Allows to select an active probe, to define a new probe, to change settings of the existing ones or to perform probe calibration procedure.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/probe_settings.PNG" width="767px" height="289px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The currently active probe is marked in blue in the list of available probes.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Set Active button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">To change the active probe, select the correct one from the list and press the button "Set Active".</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">New ... button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Allows to define a new probe by calling the following dialog:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/probe_info.PNG" width="440px" height="242px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">In this dialog the user can define:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Probe name</b></span> - type an appropriate name for the new probe</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Diameter</b></span> - input the correct probe diameter (in mm)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Type</b></span> - select the probe type. Available options are:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs7">
<col>
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top">
<td class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/Hard_Probe.png" width="61px" height="60px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs10">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/Float_Probe.png" width="88px" height="64px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs12">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/Renishaw.png" width="74px" height="66px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td class="whs14">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-weight:bold;">Hard probe</p>
</td>
<td class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-weight:bold;">Floating probe</p>
</td>
<td class="whs16">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-weight:bold;">Renishaw</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="parameterdescription">For all probe types a <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Debounce</b></span> parameter should be set. This parameter defines the minimum delay between two point captures.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Edit... button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This button allows to changes the parameters of the currently selected probe. It calls the same dialog as "New..."button, see the picture and parameters above for more details.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Delete button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Removes the currently selected probe from the list of available probes.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Calibrate button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This button starts the wizard for probe calibration. It could be applied to a new or existent probe. The whole calibration procedure is explained in details in the section <a href="../../../Probe_Calibration/Localiser_Probe_Calibration_-_Metris_MCA.htm">Probe Calibration</a>.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Check Redatum button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="background-color:Transparent;">When pressed the dialog for localiser homing appears: the procedure that sets all axes to their zero positions. If an axis is initialised its assignment is coloured in green, otherwise it appears in red.</p>
<p class="Note">Note: For a six axis arm the last axis indication is disabled (grayed).</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="../../../Localiser/Metris_MCA/arm_homing.gif" width="189px" height="407px" border="0" class="img_whs17" alt=""></p>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>:<br>
The same dialog appears at KUBE start up if the arm was not previously initialised.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">OK and Cancel button</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">OK button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Confirms the changes and returns to Hardware settings dialog.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Cancel button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Exits the dialog without keeping any changes and returns to Hardware settings dialog.</p>
